    "honest_conclusion": "The 1D axial stress-wave rod predicts a SUB-MILLISECOND tibial peak (~2L/c). It satisfies the literal V8b inequality (<=5.0 ms) only by OVERSHOOTING ~18x earlier than [T22] 4.6 ms; it does NOT reproduce the [T22] magnitude and its peak time is height-independent. This is the EXPECTED, pre-registered finding: it confirms [T22]'s 4.6 ms is CONTACT-CRUSH-controlled, not wave-controlled, and that the 6-segment chain's 5.8 ms is the closer physical match. No parameter was tuned."
